export const guide = "# 持续战役配置：准备局面，让玩家创造故事\n\n持续战役放在 `content/worlds/<id>.json`。它准备地点、人物、可取得的进展和不介入时的变化，不规定玩家必须按哪条剧情走。一级角色可以大胆创作身世，但“自称王子”“三个人穿一件斗篷”首先是人物声明；属性、动作和资源以角色卡为准。\n\n[world.schema.json](../content/world.schema.json) 是字段与取值的唯一格式合同；[world-validation.mjs](../lib/game/world-validation.mjs) 检查引用、连通性和前提关系。[月桥镇范例](../content/worlds/moonbridge-conspiracy.json) 可以直接交给 AI 参考。本文说明如何写出好玩的局面，不另定义字段。线性教学短篇仍使用 [schemaVersion 1](campaign-format.md)，两种格式不能混写。\n\n## 文件与版本\n\n配置采用 UTF-8 JSON、两空格缩进和末尾换行。固定 `$schema: \"../world.schema.json\"`、`format: \"situation-v1\"`、`schemaVersion: 2`、`rulesVersion: \"srd-5.1-table-2\"`。`id` 是稳定英文标识；修改已有内容时递增 `revision`，不要把修订号当作软件版本。\n\n`order` 决定大厅顺序；标题、简介、主题、难度和 `minutes` 是展示文案。时长应写成估计，不能用“每晚四小时、一定玩十次”承诺玩家体验。`hook` 是开场可见信息，不能包含谜底。地点数组第一项是出生点。\n\n新存档保存整份配置快照及修订号。后来增加或修订剧本，旧存档仍使用出发时的内容。新增规则版本需要引擎支持或明确迁移，不能只把字符串换成新的版本号。\n\n## 六种内容各自负责什么\n\n| 内容 | 作者准备什么 | 运行时如何使用 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `locations` | 地点描述、出入口、在场人物、安全休息条件 | 玩家可以沿 `exits` 移动和回访；未相邻地点不能瞬移 |\n| `npcs` | 名字、公开角色、想要什么、秘密、所在地点 | 当前人物的角色、欲望和有限信任展示给玩家；`secret` 不直接发给玩家或叙事模型 |\n| `clues` | 有标题与内容的真实发现 | 只有引擎实际发放后，才进入玩家和 AI 的已知事实 |\n| `objectives` | 可持续记录的世界改变 | 成功机会或时钟阈值使目标成立；仅已完成的改变公开展示，未知描述不提前发给玩家或 AI；不能由一段 AI 对话直接写入 |\n| `opportunities` | 当前局面中可能取得的进展 | 按地点与已知线索开放；玩家既可用建议方法，也可描述适合目标的新方法 |\n| `clocks` | 无人介入时怎样变化，以及什么行动能稳定局势 | 行动、失败和休息推进刻度；阈值可发放明确线索或目标，不能自行结束战役 |\n\n所有 ID 引用必须存在，各个带 `id` 的数组内部不能重名，包括 `backstoryHooks`；不使用表达式、脚本、外部 URL 指令或动态代码。NPC 的 `location` 和该地点 `npcIds` 必须一致，同一个 NPC 只能列在其声明地点。出入口是有方向的；希望双向通行就两边都写，不能假设引擎自动补路。\n\n## 一个机会的规则\n\n机会的 `prompt` 写玩家看得到的问题与一个建议方法，不写成功后的秘密。`requires` 是需要已经获得的**线索 ID**，不是目标或任意条件表达式。`skills` 声明该目标支持哪些适合的方法；当前 DC 允许 10、12、15、18。想容许更多创意，声明合理的多项技能，并让描述解释它们怎样接近目标。\n\n`success` 明确写 `text`、`clues`、`objectives`；没有奖励时用空数组。可选 `trustNpc` 只提升当前在场人物的一格态度，可选 `ending` 指向一个结局。`failure.text` 必须与失败时真实成立的状态一致；`failure.clock` 是额外耗时 0–2 格。不能写“失败也拿到了同一张秘密账本”而不配置发放，更不能把人物死亡或物品损坏只写进文案。\n\n机会的结果已经全部成立时，等效机会会关闭，避免先成功救人又被描述成救援失败。显式结局选择保留到玩家实际选择为止。失败的相同方法不能原地重掷；改用另一办法或取得相关准备后，可以重新提出裁定。准备带来的优势只消费一次。\n\n可选 `encounter` 声明一个对手，使用 schema 中支持的生命、护甲、攻击与伤害字段，可选 `sleepImmune` 明确睡眠免疫。战斗属于可选办法；给同一问题留下交涉、调查或绕行路径。当前采用单一对手与抽象站位，不能配置网格距离、群体目标或未实现的特殊攻击。胜利取得该机会的配置结果，并留在当前地点。\n\n## 时钟与结局\n\n时钟刻度是**叙事进度**，法术持续时间另按实际分钟保存。通常赶路或一次探索行动推进 1 格，失败再增加配置的额外格数；独立施法推进 1 格，仪式额外 1 格，短休 6 格，章节休整 8 格。关闭程序不会推动刻度。\n\n每个阈值有 `at` 和公开事件 `text`，可选一个 `clue`、一个 `objective`。阈值须在 `max` 内且不重复。`stoppedBy` 是目标 ID 数组，其中任意一个已完成便停止该时钟。让事件带来新线索、第三方介入或新的代价，可以防止关键骰子失败后故事停住；阈值文案必须对应实际配置效果。\n\n结局必须包含引擎保留的 `retreat`。其他结局通过某个机会的 `success.ending` **明确选择**，并可声明 `requires` 目标与 `clues` 线索。这些条件必须在选择结局前由普通机会或时钟取得，不能依赖任何结局选择完成后才发放的结果；战役结束后不能继续行动来解锁另一个结局。抵达最后一个地点、时钟走满或 AI 说“故事结束”都不会自动触发结局。条件未成立的选择不会出现。\n\n## 人物背景如何接进故事\n\n`backstoryHooks` 准备当前位置可问玩家的话题，包含位置、问题、标签和固定 `truthStatus: \"unresolved\"`。它是 DM 的谈话入口，不能凭标签向玩家发放血统能力、王位、魔法物品或世界秘密。当前标签是作者整理信息，不自动匹配人物经历或改写剧情。\n\nDM 会读取角色的性格、理想、羁绊、缺点、目标、合作理由和过去，再用这些信息扮演回应。持久事实是已知线索、目标、人物信任、时钟和已执行行动；未证实身份记录为人物声明。事件手记保留最近 300 项，聊天保留最近 180 条；长期结果保存在独立状态，不依赖把整段历史塞给模型。\n\n自由行动每次只裁定一个目的：取得当前机会、前往相邻地点、和在场人物交涉，或完成有限准备。AI 可以理解方法与提出裁定，但不能发放任意新能力、装备、金钱、伤害或隐藏真相。没有对应机会的准备成功，会为当前位置下一次同技能目标检定提供一次优势；交涉只能有限改变态度，说服不是精神控制。真实可用的探索法术才可参与行动，确认后才消耗资源。\n\n## 生成、检查、试玩\n\n把 [持续战役生成提示词](world-generation-prompt.txt)、schema 与范例同时交给 AI；只接收配置文件，不让模型改写引擎。生成后先单文件校验，再加入仓库：\n\n```sh\nnode scripts/content-workflow.mjs --file content/worlds/my-adventure.json\nnpm run content:sync\nnpm run content:check\nnpm test\nnpx tsc --noEmit\n```\n\n依赖检查会计入机会与时钟阈值可能提供的线索和目标，并排除结局用自身结果解锁自己的循环；它不模拟所有移动顺序、提前停钟与其他动态分支。格式检查不会证明故事有趣，也不能证明每个动态路径都畅通。至少试玩一条成功路线、一条连续失败路线、一次主动回访、一次违背 NPC 意愿的请求，以及每个结局的真实行动流程。检查的重点是：奖励是否实际发放、文案是否与状态一致、失败后是否还有有意义的选择、休息时世界是否仍会变化。\n";
export const prompt = "You author ORIGINAL Chinese tabletop situations for Lantern Table. Return exactly one UTF-8 JSON object. No markdown fence, commentary, scripts, expressions, arbitrary extra fields, or engine changes.\n\nInputs required: content/world.schema.json, docs/world-format.md, and content/worlds/moonbridge-conspiracy.json. If these inputs are missing, request them rather than inventing fields. The JSON schema is the sole structural contract; the format guide explains runtime semantics. Target format=\"situation-v1\", schemaVersion=2, rulesVersion=\"srd-5.1-table-2\", $schema=\"../world.schema.json\". A new ID is stable lowercase kebab-case. revision is an integer >=1 and increments for edits.\n\nDesign situations, not a compulsory sequence. Begin at locations[0]. All locations must be reachable from it along authored directed exits. Add reverse exits explicitly when intended. IDs must be unique within each array, including backstoryHooks. Prepare distinct NPC desires, constraints, and secrets; make public role/want and location description interesting without revealing secret truth. List each NPC exactly in its declared location's npcIds and never in another location. NPC secrets are not sent to the narrator; any reveal needed for play must be represented by an obtainable clue and an explicit opportunity or clock threshold.\n\nPrefer 6-12 revisit-able locations, 6-12 distinct NPCs, and 15-35 meaningful opportunities for a multi-session Level1 situation. These are creative targets, not mandatory schema limits. Duration is an honest estimate, never a promise of a fixed marathon. Provide several agendas players can pursue, competing interests, meaningful tradeoffs, safe locations for regrouping, and more than one method to resolve major problems. No copyrighted published adventure plot or proprietary character.\n\nFor each opportunity: id/location/title/prompt/skills/dc/requires/success/failure are required. The prompt is a visible problem and suggested method, not a hidden answer. Requires refers ONLY to clue IDs. Supported skills: athletics,acrobatics,sleightOfHand,stealth,arcana,history,investigation,nature,religion,animalHandling,insight,medicine,perception,survival,deception,intimidation,performance,persuasion. DC must be 10,12,15,18. Include several defensible skills where creative methods should be possible. success requires text/clues/objectives; use empty arrays if none. Optional trustNpc must be present here. Optional ending must refer to a declared ending. failure requires text and clock (integer0..2 additional time). Text must match actual effects: failure cannot silently award a clue, kill a person, grant an item, inflict unsupported damage, change a location, or end play. Success cannot grant unconfigured rewards.\n\nClues/objectives are ID dictionaries, not prose assertions. Every reference must exist as an own dictionary key. Avoid circular unavailable clue prerequisites. Each significant objective should have a recoverable noncombat path or a plausible clock intervention. Equivalently completed opportunities close automatically; final ending opportunities remain explicit choices. Optional encounter uses ONLY schema-supported fields, a single living opponent in abstract positions and an alternate noncombat method. sleepImmune, when supported by the supplied schema, should be true for undead or magically sleep-immune enemies. No custom boss scripts, grid combat, arbitrary spells, or unsupported conditions.\n\nClocks represent story progress, not elapsed real-time. Author 2-4 distinct pressures that create developments rather than only punishing delay. at is unique and <=max; thresholds can explicitly grant one clue and/or one objective. Include a plausible route out of bad luck: waiting may reveal a new source or intervention, at a cost reflected in text. stoppedBy names objective IDs; any one completed stops that clock. A threshold never automatically chooses an ending. An event text must not claim unconfigured resource or world-state changes.\n\nendings must include retreat. Other endings need an opportunity with success.ending and a realizable path satisfying ending.requires (objectiveIDs) and ending.clues (clueIDs) BEFORE that opportunity is selected. Earlier non-ending opportunities or clock thresholds must supply these prerequisites; rewards from any final choice cannot unlock itself or a later choice because play stops at an ending. Clock-produced clues may be prerequisites of later opportunities. The static dependency check treats valid clock thresholds as potential producers; still verify actual timing, stoppedBy and directed travel in a real action route. Endings should resolve different values or costs, not just good/bad based on one die. Arrival at the council or final location alone cannot end the campaign.\n\nbackstoryHooks are prompts for the player at named locations, with tags and truthStatus=\"unresolved\". They may invite a claimed divine origin, noble identity, unusual appearance, personal bond or flaw, but never establish it as objective truth or grant mechanical powers. Personality, ideal, bond, flaw, goal and cooperation are supplied by the player's separate character card. Do not put player-specific facts into campaign configuration.\n\nRuntime boundaries: AI parses purpose and METHOD, asks one clarification when needed, explains impossible requests without rolling, and proposes one bounded action. Rules own DC, dice, rewards, resources, prerequisites and endings. Generic free actions only prepare an advantage for the next same-skill target check in the current location, move along an adjacent exit, or change a present NPC's trust one step. Persuasion does not compel surrender of a kingdom. A natural20 does not guarantee skill success. Background is a claim. Available spells are the actual card's supported repertoire, not fictional powers implied by backstory. A failed unchanged method cannot be rerolled; actual relevant preparation allows one retry.\n\nBefore returning: verify required fields, no unknown fields, own references, directed reachability, NPC placement, clue dependency reachability, finite enemy stats, stoppedBy refs, threshold range/duplicates, all ending choices and prerequisites. For each finale describe a valid action route internally, and simulate repeated failures: identify the next meaningful alternative. Do not include this analysis in the JSON. Format with two-space indentation and a final newline.\n";
